    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Stepping into the center of the hotel lobby with a microphone, Denis declares his love to Katya on one knee—just as Senya and Fedya tip the box over the balcony and shower the crowd in Madagascar cockroaches. Listen to the dramatic moment.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дай мне микрофон на минуту.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "С тех пор мы всегда вместе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты наполняешь мою жизнь смыслом!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Вика, смотри, что он делает!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты моя жизнь!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты мой мир!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты мне очень нужна, Катя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Что ты делаешь, Денис?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я сейчас всё тебе скажу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Катя, выходи за меня!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Что это падает сверху?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Откуда здесь эти тараканы?!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дай мне микрофон на минуту.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Give me the microphone for a minute.' The meaning hinges on 'give' working together with 'a minute' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "С тех пор мы всегда вместе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Since then we have always been together.' In Russian, the idea of 'with' flows naturally into 'together' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты наполняешь мою жизнь смыслом!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You fill my life with meaning!' Denis anchors the line on 'you', while 'with meaning' completes the thought. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Вика, смотри, что он делает!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vika, look what he is doing!' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'Vika' and 'watch' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты моя жизнь!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are my life!' In Russian, the idea of 'you' flows naturally into 'life' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты мой мир!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are my world!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'you' and finishing on 'world'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты мне очень нужна, Катя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I need you so much, Katya.' Denis anchors the line on 'you', while 'Katya' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Что ты делаешь, Денис?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What are you doing, Denis?' The grammar packs 'what' and 'Denis' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я сейчас всё тебе скажу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will tell you everything right now.' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'will say' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Катя, выходи за меня!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Katya, marry me!' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Katya' before landing on 'me'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Что это падает сверху?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What is that falling from above?' The meaning hinges on 'what' working together with 'upstairs' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Откуда здесь эти тараканы?!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where did these cockroaches come from?!' Notice how Russian expresses 'where from' and 'cockroaches' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
